From 65ecfad864dbf7d42b156493dd081016a1e84023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:47:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Review fixes for zero copy and the VU thread

From a review of 0146-0151:
- Zero copy stopping mid-run (an image that cannot be created or exported)
  left the shown shared image's slot taken: the readback ring stalled and
  the picture froze. A read-back frame now retires it.
- A shared image the window cannot import: zero copy now stops for good
  (ga2_pgs::disableZeroCopy) instead of the slot never being shown and its
  binary semaphore being signalled twice; shared frames replaced unseen are
  released once zero copy is off. The fd goes back (closed) when OpenGL
  refuses the import. GA2_ZEROCOPY_FAIL_AT=<n> makes the n-th import fail
  (checked: 4x at a 175 cap keeps showing frames by read-back, none
  dropped).
- VU thread (opt-in): a CSR DIRECT that began in an earlier pass was split
  with that pass's chunk index; such a pass now runs on the game thread
  whole. After a resync in the middle of a DIRECT its end counts as CSR
  (the bytes already gone are unknown). A tick job that throws is still
  counted, so the next tick cannot wait forever.

ps2x_tests 641/641, gs_cache 45/45; VU thread frames unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
